  "_doc": "v1 (PostureV1) dataset split, recovered from the training repo so v1 vs v2 can be compared on the same held-out data. Source: 'FORMIQ Form Analysis Model/data/squat_processed/user_level_multilabel_splits.json'. Splits are USER-LEVEL (one video per user, 1625 users), so no SUBJECT appears in both train and test. NOTE (G-44/G-45): user-level is NOT content-level. The corpus holds 105 byte-identical duplicate videos filed under different names, 45 of them spanning splits and 104 filed under different user ids, so identical CONTENT does appear in both. 27 of the 224 videos in the published evaluation have a byte-identical twin in train. The split data below is unchanged and correct as a user-level partition; only this description was overclaiming. See bench/results/2026-09-23-corpus-duplicates.md.",
